{"answers":[{"question_id":"Q019_stable_periodic_release_semantics","answer":"The current-release endpoint (/api/v1/releases/current) reports SCOPe 2.08 as the current public release, with stable_label "2.08-stable" and a latest_periodic_update of version "2.08-2026-08-16" dated 2026-08-16. The 2.08 release was frozen on 2021-07-28 and released on 2021-09-22; it is flagged is_public=true and is_comprehensive=false (i.e., it does not classify every PDB entry), and old_version is null.

For a reproducible analysis you should cite the exact release identifier plus the periodic-update label actually used: at minimum pin release "2.08" explicitly in every call (e.g. /api/v1/releases/2.08/...), and record the specific stable or periodic label ("2.08-stable" or "2.08-2026-08-16") together with the fetch date. Do not rely on the unqualified "current" endpoint in a methods section, because it is a moving pointer: both the designated current release and its latest periodic update can change over time, so the same query may return different content later.

The "periodic" label denotes an incremental, automatically generated update to the 2.08 release series: new PDB entries and chains are added to the frozen 2.08 classification hierarchy using automated methods (sequence and structure matching to existing manually curated 2.08 domains) without changing the curated classification of the stable 2.08 nodes. Fold/superfamily/family node definitions, SUNIDs and SCCS identifiers of the stable release remain unchanged; what the periodic update adds is extra automatically classified entries and derived similarity evidence (e.g., chain/AlphaFold hit streams) as of the update date embedded in the version string. In contrast, "2.08-stable" denotes the fixed, manually curated 2021 freeze. Periodic updates therefore carry weaker curation guarantees than the stable release (automated assignments are candidate evidence, not manual curation), and analyses that depend on them must cite the dated periodic label, not just "2.08", because later periodic updates of the same series will contain more or different entries.","evidence_used":["mcp__scope__get_scop_service_info","/api/v1/","/api/v1/releases/current"]}]}
